    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L11-ACTIVITY-001",
      "SourceSection": "11.1: Math Talk: Finding Values",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\log \\frac{1}{1,000}\\)",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L11-ACTIVITY-002",
      "SourceSection": "11.2: Log War!",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Have you played the game of war with a deck of playing cards?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L11-ACTIVITY-003",
      "SourceSection": "11.2: Log War!",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Your teacher will give you and your partner a set of special cards.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L11-ACTIVITY-004",
      "SourceSection": "11.2: Log War!",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Shuffle and deal the cards evenly.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L11-ACTIVITY-005",
      "SourceSection": "11.2: Log War!",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Each player turns one card face up. The card with the greater value wins the round and its player captures both cards and sets them aside.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L11-ACTIVITY-006",
      "SourceSection": "11.2: Log War!",
      "SourceExcerpt": "If you and your partner disagree about the value of a card, discuss until you reach an agreement.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L11-ACTIVITY-007",
      "SourceSection": "11.2: Log War!",
      "SourceExcerpt": "If there is a tie, each player turns another card face up. The player whose card has the greater value captures all cards (including the cards that tie).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L11-ACTIVITY-008",
      "SourceSection": "11.2: Log War!",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Play until all the cards are turned up. The player with the most cards wins.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L11-ACTIVITY-009",
      "SourceSection": "11.2: Log War!",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Let the logarithm war begin!",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L11-ACTIVITY-010",
      "SourceSection": "11.2: Log War!",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Mai uses the fact that \\(\\sqrt[3]{2}\\) is close to 1.25 and that \\(2^3=8\\) to make the estimate \\(\\log_2(10) \\approx 3\\frac{1}{3}\\). Explain Mai’s estimate. How exact is the estimate?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L11-ACTIVITY-011",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: Finding Logarithms with a Calculator",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Experiment with your calculator until you understand how to evaluate \\(\\log_{10} 19\\). What value do you see on the calculator?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L11-ACTIVITY-012",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: Finding Logarithms with a Calculator",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Discuss with a partner: Why might \\(\\log_{10} 19\\) be expressed in different ways?",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L11-ACTIVITY-013",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: Finding Logarithms with a Calculator",
      "SourceExcerpt": "To solve the equation \\(10^m= 19\\), Tyler writes the equation in the logarithmic form: \\(m = \\log_{10} 19\\). He then presses the “log” button on the calculator, enters the number “19,” and writes down an approximation of 1.279. Priya…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L11-ACTIVITY-014",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: Finding Logarithms with a Calculator",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Express the solution to each equation using a logarithm. Next, find the approximate value of the solution using a calculator.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L11-ACTIVITY-015",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: Finding Logarithms with a Calculator",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Estimate the value of each expression. Explain to a partner how you made your estimate. Next, check your estimate with a calculator.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L11-ACTIVITY-016",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: Finding Logarithms with a Calculator",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Sometimes it’s possible to find an exact value for a logarithm. For example \\(\\log_2 0.125 = \\text{-}3\\) because \\(0.125 = \\frac18\\) and \\(2^{\\text{-}3} = \\frac18\\). Similarly, \\(\\log_5 625 = 4\\) because \\(5^4 = 625\\).",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L11-ACTIVITY-017",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: Finding Logarithms with a Calculator",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Often times it is not possible to find an exact value, but using number sense allows us to get a reasonable estimate. Let’s say we want to find \\(x\\) that makes \\(10^x = 980\\) true.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L11-ACTIVITY-018",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: Finding Logarithms with a Calculator",
      "SourceExcerpt": "We can first express \\(x\\) as \\(\\log_{10} 980\\). Because 980 is between \\(10^2\\) and \\(10^3\\)\\(, \\) \\(\\log_{10} 980\\) is between 2 and 3.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L11-ACTIVITY-019",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: Finding Logarithms with a Calculator",
      "SourceExcerpt": "But where does \\(\\log_{10} 980\\) lie between 2 and 3? Because 980 is much closer to 1,000 than it is to 100, \\(\\log_{10} 980\\) is likely a lot closer to 3 than it is to 2. This means 2.9 would be a better estimate than 2.1 would be.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L11-ACTIVITY-020",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: Finding Logarithms with a Calculator",
      "SourceExcerpt": "We can use a calculator to verify our estimate and find that \\(\\log_{10} 980\\) is very close to 3, about 2.99.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U04-L11-ACTIVITY-021",
      "SourceSection": "11.3: Finding Logarithms with a Calculator",
      "SourceExcerpt": "The logarithm to base 10 of a number \\(x\\), written \\(\\log_{10}(x)\\), is the exponent you raise 10 to get \\(x\\), so it is the number \\(y\\) that makes the equation \\(10^y = x\\) true. Logarithms to other bases are defined the same way with…",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u04-l11.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
